    "rationale": "Only one defensible compositional paradigm is supported. The forms brF, coldF, hotF, and dimF show a clear substitution set in the shared frame _ + F, where the first slot contributes a property ('bright'/'cold'/'hot'/'dim') and F contributes 'face'. Their whole meanings are predictable from the parts. The suggested ce and fa families fail the semantic-consistency and shared-frame tests, and F1–F6 are best treated as opaque indexed lexemes rather than F + numeral.",
